### US-03 / US-04 · The local collection
# Reads are public. Sync, edit and delete need a bearer token: run the first request (or auth.http) first.

### Sign in as demo and keep the token
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/sign-in
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "demo",
  "password": "demo1234"
}

> {% client.global.set("token", response.body.token); %}

### Browse the collection (seeded with Bulbasaur … Caterpie)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/stored-pokemon?page=0&size=20

### View one stored Pokémon
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/stored-pokemon/1

### Not in the collection — 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/stored-pokemon/150

### Copy Pikachu from PokeAPI into the collection — 201 the first time, 200 (refreshed) after that
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/stored-pokemon/25/sync
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Sync without signing in — 401
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/stored-pokemon/25/sync

### Set our own fields (full replace; fields left out are cleared)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/stored-pokemon/25
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "localizedName": "ピカチュウ",
  "region": "Kanto",
  "tags": ["electric", "starter", "favourite"]
}

### Invalid own fields: blank name, duplicate tags — 400 with invalidFields
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/stored-pokemon/25
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "localizedName": "   ",
  "region": "Kanto",
  "tags": ["electric", "electric"]
}

### Remove Pikachu from the collection — 204
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/stored-pokemon/25
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
